<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-12">
  <header class="text-center mb-16">
    <h1 class="text-5xl font-black tracking-tight mb-4">About <span class="text-primary">WWWorkRemote</span></h1>
    <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-500">Founded &amp; Engineered by Mike Hall</p>
  </header>

  <div class="space-y-12">
    <section class="card-neural p-10">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-blue-400 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-blue-400"></span> Origins
      </h2>
      <div class="prose-invert text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        <p class="mb-4 text-white font-bold">WWWorkRemote was founded and created by Mike Hall.</p>
        <p class="mb-4">The project was born out of Mike's necessity to cut through the noise of the global remote job market. What started as a series of foundational Ruby scripts has evolved into a job aggregation and career-management app designed to ingest, normalize, and intelligently categorize job postings from across the web.</p>
        <p>Mike established the vision and laid the critical groundwork: a high-density, vector-indexed repository that empowers developers to find their next role without the friction of traditional job boards.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card-neural p-10 border-l-4 border-l-primary">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-primary mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-primary"></span> AI Collaboration
      </h2>
      <div class="prose-invert text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        <p class="mb-4">In 2026, Mike expanded the project's capabilities through collaboration with AI coding agents. Working with these agents, the project transitioned to a local-first LLM architecture.</p>
        <p class="mb-4">While AI agents assisted in refining the interface and implementing the high-concurrency Fiber-based async architecture, the system remains anchored in Mike's original design for operational independence and data privacy.</p>
        <p>Using local models via llama.cpp, WWWorkRemote performs classification, sentiment analysis, and tech-stack extraction on-premise, realizing Mike's vision for a self-sufficient job intelligence engine.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card-neural p-10 border-t border-white/5 bg-gradient-to-br from-base-200 to-base-300">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span> The Stack
      </h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 font-mono text-sm font-bold text-slate-500">
        <div class="p-4 bg-white/5 rounded border border-white/5">
          <div class="mb-1 text-slate-500">Backend</div>
          <div class="text-white">Rails 8</div>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-white/5 rounded border border-white/5">
          <div class="mb-1 text-slate-500">AI Framework</div>
          <div class="text-white">RubyLLM</div>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-white/5 rounded border border-white/5">
          <div class="mb-1 text-slate-500">Vector Database</div>
          <div class="text-white">PgVector</div>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-white/5 rounded border border-white/5">
          <div class="mb-1 text-slate-500">Theme</div>
          <div class="text-white">Kanagawa Wave</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="text-center pt-8">
      <%= link_to root_path, class: "text-sm font-bold text-slate-500 hover:text-white transition-colors" do %>
        &larr; Back to Dashboard
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
